' 4+1 process view - Pipeline of an API request · the order in Program.cs
' Version 1.1 - 2026-11-10
' For: whoever writes code and whoever debugs.
' Documented decision: The order of a request's middlewares is that of Api/Program.cs.
' Not drawn: internal detail of the classes.
@startuml process-pipeline
!include ../style.puml

title Process view - pipeline of an API request: the order in Program.cs

start
:HTTP request to the API
(from the Next.js rewrites or, in development, straight to port 5080);
note right
  WebApplication adds UseRouting before the middlewares
  in Program.cs: the endpoint is already chosen, so the
  following middlewares read its attributes
  ([EnableRateLimiting], [AllowAnonymous], [Authorize]).
end note
:UseForwardedHeaders
the client IP comes from X-Forwarded-For only when the connection
comes from ForwardedHeaders:KnownProxies / KnownNetworks;
:UseResponseSecurityHeaders
X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff on every response,
also on the errors and refusals that come next;
:UseExceptionHandler and UseStatusCodePages
wrap everything that follows;
if (UseOriginCheck
POST, PUT, PATCH or DELETE without an accepted Origin?) then (yes)
  :403 origin_not_allowed;
  stop
else (no)
endif
if (UseRateLimiter
does the endpoint have [EnableRateLimiting]
and is the IP's window (/64 on IPv6) used up?) then (yes)
  :429 too_many_requests
  with Retry-After;
  stop
else (no)
endif
:Swagger UI and /openapi (Development only);
:UseAuthentication
JwtBearer reads the access_token cookie
(without going to the database);
if (UseAuthorization
no session on an endpoint without [AllowAnonymous]?) then (yes)
  :401 unauthorized;
  stop
elseif (session of a profile that the endpoint's
policy does not accept?) then (yes)
  :403 forbidden;
  stop
else (passes)
endif
:Controller (API component) → service (Application)
returns Result<T>;
if (ServiceError?) then (yes)
  :this.Problem(error)
  ProblemDetails with code and traceId;
else (no)
  :2xx;
endif
note right
  An unhandled exception goes up to
  GlobalExceptionHandler:
  Error log and 500 internal_error.
end note
stop
@enduml
